WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.167
Tucker Carlson has been shown

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.469
the door at Fox News.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.303
We've been learning more

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.371
about the kind of workplace

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.538
he allegedly fostered.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.773
Some of it comes from his former

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.274
head, booker, Abby Grossberg.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.909
She's filed a pair of lawsuits

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.177
against Fox in Delaware

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.046
and in federal court here in New York.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:13.747
We should also mention

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:14.814
she worked for this program

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.950
in 2007 as an associate producer.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.286
She and I spoke just before airtime

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:21.855
when you heard

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.056
that Tucker Carlson got fired.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.958
Did you feel vindicated? In a way?

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.127
In a way, I did. First, it was a shock.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.262
So there's obviously a lot to process

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.063
You didn't expect that

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.131
they would do that?

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.400
I didn't believe people when they told me

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:33.867
because I

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.335
because he had so much power

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.403
at the network.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.570
I thought he was invincible.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.072
I thought his team was invincible.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.640
And they believe they were, too,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.342
by the way that they behaved.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:45.512
You say in in two of your lawsuits,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.347
you say that

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.515
you endured a work

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.083
environment quote, work environment

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.151
that subjugates women

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.318
based on vile, sexist

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.820
stereotypes, typecast,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.321
religious minorities,

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.556
belittles their traditions

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.257
and demonstrates

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.291
little to no regard

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.527
for those suffering from mental illness.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.728
In the lawsuit, you say Mr.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.329
Carlson's derogatory comments

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:03.930
toward women

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.664
and his disdain

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.899
for those who dare to object

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.367
to such misogyny is well known.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.035
On the set of Tucker Carlson tonight.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.471
His attitude,

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:11.938
what you see

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.772
are his attitudes

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.141
that permeated the culture at his show.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:15.608
Of course.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.377
And I think the best example of

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.179
that was when I ultimately

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.580
and I'm jumping ahead,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.348
did stand up and complain

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.117
to one of my supervisors.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.018
His answer to me

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.086
was Tucker

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.487
sets the tone for the show,

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.556
and we follow Tucker's tone.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.658
And that summarizes everything.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.828
So people got a message from Tucker

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.930
Carlson that it was okay to

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.997
use the C word

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.599
or whatever it was,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.701
and they felt emboldened to do that, too.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.237
I think that they took pride

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.405
and joy in doing it.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.539
They thought it was fun.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.775
It was just really kind of a bro fest

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.542
there.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.977
It's also incredible,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.413
your descriptions of the.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.047
I don't know

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.682
if it's he was always like this

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.817
or his ratings and power

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.153
went to his head. But from what you say,

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.522
he talks as if he was in

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.090
the position to

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.258
destroy campaigns

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.061
and would actually threaten politicians.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:08.661
Like if you don't

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.262
come on the show,

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.663
we're going to have some congressmen.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.231
If you don't come on

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:11.631
the show,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.600
we're going to destroy your campaign.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.801
Shocking to me.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.369
His lieutenant, Justin Wells,

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.804
who was fired along with him

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.872
I have messages

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.373
I was just looking at today saying

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.408
we are the most powerful

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.743
political platform

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.311
in the Republican Party.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.646
And they acted that way,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.348
especially leading up to the 20,

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.450
22 midterms.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.252
They would say

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.220
there was like Ron Johnson, for example,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.855
the office called me and said,

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:36.656
he'll come on the show,

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.724
but are you going to destroy him?

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.092
Because this will ruin his chances.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.860
It will be over for him.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.662
So the politicians were terrified of it.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.563
Yeah, they were.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.098
And that was a power that

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.433
I was terrified of, too.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.235
I don't think journalists should have

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.937
that kind of power

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.405
to threaten and bully people.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.407
And Tucker did and reveled in it.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.242
He enjoyed that.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.311
That was part of his persona.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:58.811
Yeah.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.380
I mean, they believed that

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.749
he could broker who was speaker.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.483
House speaker.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.951
He wanted to do that live on air.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.420
But Kevin McCarthy said no,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.321
What do you mean

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.223
he wanted to do that live on air?

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.959
His plan was to have Kevin McCarthy

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:13.793
come on the show.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.662
According to

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.629
Justin Wells, reveal

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.598
this grand plan to us.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.365
Tucker, a few days

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.634
earlier had sort of set some terms

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.771
for McCarthy, which included this church

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:27.273
kind of committee that he said about

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.841
I think this was about January 5th.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.343
So about January 2nd,

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.345
he said,
you should have this church committee.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.013
So fast forward to January 5th.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.815
They started asking me to book McCarthy

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:36.649
on the show that night.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.484
I had worked with him

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:38.985
a lot

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.353
when I was a Sunday morning futures

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.055
and had a relationship with his team.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.691
That afternoon, Justin came in

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.226
and he said, Here's the plan.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.361
Tucker is going to first have Kevin on.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.463
Hear him beg and grovel.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.165
Then we'll bring in Matt Gates.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.700
And Matt Gates will

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.668
then kind of set his terms

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.570
Then Tucker will set his terms

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.339
that McCarthy has to agree to

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.107
for Carlson had terms to the.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.642
Yeah, terms.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.544
And we're going to make this whole thing

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.211
happen on air

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.013
and save the Republican Party.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.616
Now, fortunately, for McCarthy's sake,

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:10.817
he said no.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.285
But he did call Tucker

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:12.752
the next day

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.553
from his office

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.655
with Representative Thomas Massie,

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.890
and had agreed to some of Tucker's terms,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.092
according to a text

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.360
that Tucker had sent me.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.462
And he said that was a win.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.696
Prior to working for Carlson,

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.432
you worked on Maria Bartiromo show.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.035
She repeatedly had Sidney Powell

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:32.105
on Rudy Giuliani on spreading lies.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.607
When you were a senior producer,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:37.076
there Was that okay with you? Did you.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.946
Did you buy into that?

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.981
It's an interesting thing to look back on

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.083
from kind of a perch of perspective now.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.519
But being there in the moment,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.055
I was definitely seduced for about a week

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:49.922
by those ideas

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.191
as tens of millions of Americans

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.160
were and wondering

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.928
if there could be evidence.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.196
And I was waiting for it

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.097
and waiting for it

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:58.698
because the president

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.432
of the United States

00:04:59.432 --> 00:04:59.799
had made

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.535
very serious claims of fraud

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.971
and that evidence never came.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:07.840
So for me, it took a few days to kind of

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:09.809
just realize

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:12.412
that the whole thing was a ruse and

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.449
a kind of you know,

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.451
I think the American public

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.385
was also waiting

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.787
and coming to that realization

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.422
around the same time.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:23.656
And Fox

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:24.757
certainly fueled

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:25.992
that false hope for them.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.261
But but I mean, plenty of people

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.797
were saying there is no there there.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.432
Did you feel an obligation?

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:34.667
I mean,
Maria Bartiromo did not

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.536
push back on Sidney Powell

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:38.638
or Rudy Giuliani.

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.606
Did you feel an obligation to like

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:41.974
get in her ear and say,

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.176
you got to push back?

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:43.910
Yeah.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.445
And I had statements

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.313
and I had statements.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.549
And you would put up a deposition,

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.084
a Dominion statement

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.885
at one point on the screen,

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.420
and she didn't read it.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.522
Ultimately, it was up to her to read it

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.523
and she didn't.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.926
And those were pre tapes as well.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.694
And all the executives at Fox

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:02.261
were watching

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.897
them come in and saw no problem with it.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.399
Their only concern was that

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.201
perhaps Rudy would come on

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:11.404
and bash Fox for calling Arizona first.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:12.905
You've said it in

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:13.740
some of your interviews

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.541
that you you were in the bubble.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.075
I want to hear.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.110
You said you were in the bubble.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:17.977
You were talking with the Trump

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:19.145
White House during COVID.

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:19.946
You were get, quote,

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.847
getting my information

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.215
from people that were close to Trump

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.716
and also running a show by myself.

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.018
I mean,
did you not feel

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.553
you had a journalistic obligation?

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:28.755
I mean, you could have

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:29.956
there were plenty of other people

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.057
to talk to other than Trump

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:32.759
people to get facts.

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.393
No,

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:34.794
there were

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:35.595
those were the people

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:37.697
that Maria ultimately wanted on the show

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.065
and the Fox executives

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.299
okayed to be on the show.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.902
So but there was never a feeling of like,

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:43.770
were there discussions

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.271
with Maria Bartiromo

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:48.741
about, should I push back on this person?

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.042
Should I?

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.812
You know, there's there's I mean,

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:53.913
there's plenty of evidence

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.516
there is no election fraud.

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.851
Why not have Maria Bartiromo

00:06:58.851 --> 00:06:59.519
say that

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:00.953
to Sidney Powell or like,

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.221
where's your actual proof?

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.823
Or She was supposed to.

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.124
It was in the notes.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:06.359
It was her responsibility

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:08.594
ultimately to do that. And she didn't.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:09.729
And it was the

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.564
role of the executives at Fox

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.365
who were watching that

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:13.299
come in live,

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:16.335
David Clarke and Jay Wallace, to say,

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.170
we're not going to re-air

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:18.571
this or we're going to cut this out.

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.406
And ultimately, they didn't.

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:22.341
And when I was deposed

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.409
in the Dominion case,

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.711
I was told to downplay the fact

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:26.779
that I didn't have help.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:27.980
And I was asking for help.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.749
Never to say that,

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:30.850
never to pin the blame

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.885
on those executives who were mouths

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.821
that they ultimately had

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:36.656
responsibility over the content

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.424
that ended up on the air.

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:39.992
And to just sort of say,

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:42.094
I didn't remember what had happened.

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.363
Do you believe that

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.598
you had a responsibility

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:47.934
to point out something that was not true,

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:49.235
that it was said on your air?

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.102
Absolutely.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:50.970
And Maria

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.004
had a responsibility

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:52.772
to push back,

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.240
which she ultimately didn't do

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.908
and should have said,

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:57.109
why do you think she didn't?

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:58.311
Did she just believe in this

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.011
or did

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.646
she just know where the ratings were

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.882
and what her audience wanted?

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:05.051
I've thought a lot about this and

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:06.652
having known her

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:08.788
and it worked with her very closely,

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:10.556
I do think she believed it

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.924
And I think it was also

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:14.160
a result of the misogyny at the network

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.429
and them just pushing her further

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:17.396
and further

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:18.197
into the corner

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.432
where she had to had

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:21.200
bigger and bigger news,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.336
which was very much contingent

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:24.504
on Trump winning.

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.038
And she had a lot of hope

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:27.006
that he could pull that

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:28.241
through till the very end.

00:08:28.241 --> 00:08:28.741
But isn't it

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:30.943
her job to have some

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:32.144
sense of responsibility?

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.379
And like in the end,

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.248
if you're being pushed to say stuff

